#! mathcas 2 notebook

#% title
# convolve

#% text
# `convolve(f, g, x, y)` gives the convolution of f and g: `integrate(f(x) g(y - x), [x, -inf, inf])` as a function of y.

#% section
# Details

#% item
# Piecewise polynomials with rational interval bounds convolve to a piecewise polynomial in y.

#% item
# The value is that of `integrate`, simplified; convergence conditions it reports are kept.

#% section
# Examples

#% subsection
# Basic examples

#% cell
convolve(dirac_delta(x), f(x), x, y)
#% output
#= f(y)

#% cell
convolve(exp(-a*x^2), 1, x, y)
#% output
#= conditional_expression(pi^(1/2)/a^(1/2), re(a) > 0)

#% section
# See also

#% text
# `integrate`, `fourier_transform`
